  "id": "Compound::DB01197 - Gene::6564",
  "verbalization": "Captopril, a common ACE inhibitor, is linked to Slc15a1 through a shared mechanism involving Fosinopril, an ACE inhibitor with similar pharmacological properties. The evidence suggests that Captopril causes a range of developmental disorders, including Skull Hypoplasia, Oligohydramnios, and Microsomia, all of which are associated with Fosinopril. These conditions are mediated by Fosinopril's ability to bind to Slc15a1, a gene involved in cellular transport and function. The lowest common ancestor of Captopril and Fosinopril is identified as an L-Proline Derivative, which is a common component of ACE inhibitors, reinforcing the shared pathway. The consistent association between Captopril and Slc15a1, through Fosinopril, highlights a pharmacological dependency where the inhibition of ACE by these drugs leads to downstream effects on Slc15a1, potentially impacting cellular processes. This relationship underscores the role of ACE inhibitors in modulating gene expression through their shared metabolic pathways.",
